            </Main>
            <RURComments xml:space="preserve">
                <airSeal>During the infiltration test, we noticed some air leakage on the following:

- All windows

- Both front and rear doors

- Attic hatch

- Electric receptacles

- Combustion air supply

The result showed a high level of air changing per hour. We recommend increasing the sealing of the building.

</airSeal>
                <mainWalls>At the time of the inspection, we noticed that the insulation level was estimated to be R-19. This insulation value is far under the actual standard of R-28. 

We recommend increasing the level of insulation to meet the actual standard.

</mainWalls>
                <ceilings>At the time of the inspection, the roof insulation thickness was 8'' which is estimated to be R-28. The attic insulation is far under the actual standard of R-60.

We recommend adding insulation to meet the standard.

</ceilings>
                <foundation>During the inspection, we noticed that the insulation of the floor above the crawl space is estimated to be R-10. We notice the presence of 2'' of rigid foam XTSP. 

We recommend adding insulation to meet the actual standard.

</foundation>
                <windows>At the time of the audit, we noticed that the windows latches were broken, and the windows remained open and therefore, cooled down the house.</windows>
                <doors>At the time of the inspection, we noticed that the exterior doors are leaky around the door knob and on the lower section.  . </doors>
            </RURComments>
        </Options>
